                "difficulty": "medium",
                "question": "<p class=\"image\"><img alt=\"Images\" class=\"q-img\" src=\"images/f0219-01.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 10px 0; display: block;\"/></p><p class=\"ques\"><strong><a href=\"ch19d.xhtml#rch19qa1_11\" id=\"ch19qa1_11\">11.</a></strong> A student pushes a big 16-kg box across the floor at constant speed. He pushes with a force of 50 N angled 35° from the horizontal, as shown in the diagram above. If the student pulls rather than pushes the box at the same angle, while maintaining a constant speed, what will happen to the force of friction?</p>",
